"""Unseen applied midterm and complete-programme final questions.
Original hypothetical questions; not copied from practice or module assessments.
"""
EXAM_ROWS=[]
def exam(module, paper, text):
    EXAM_ROWS.append(dict(module=module,paper=paper,text=text))

exam(22,'midterm','A claimant proves a breach but cannot identify the legal competence of the chosen tribunal. What should the memorandum conclude?|Merits are not enough; the forum basis still needs verification|Proof of breach creates jurisdiction automatically|Consent by the claimant makes every forum competent|An administrative office becomes appellate through convenience|Competence and substantive entitlement are separate requirements.')
exam(22,'midterm','An appellate opinion discusses three issues but resolves only one. How should the student identify its controlling rule?|Connect the necessary reasoning to the issue actually decided|Treat every broad remark as an identical holding|Use only the final party names|Assume the losing party argument is the ratio|Precedential reasoning must be located in its decisional context.')
exam(22,'midterm','Two decisions involve debt, but only the earlier one establishes a personal undertaking. What improves the comparison?|Explain whether the undertaking was material to the earlier reasoning|Assume all debt cases impose personal liability|Ignore the undertaking because both parties owe money|Distinguish only because the cases occurred in different years|A relevant distinction concerns facts on which the legal reasoning depends.')
exam(22,'midterm','A court-access plan identifies travel and language barriers but no filing requirements. What should be added?|The lawful entry process and required documents for the competent forum|A promise that practical difficulty removes every requirement|A foreign court fee as an automatic local rule|An instruction to obtain a private judgment from any official|Practical access and proper procedure must be planned together.')
exam(23,'midterm','A memo question says the employer was definitely dishonest before analysis begins. What revision is best?|Frame a neutral issue tied to the relevant conduct and rule|Repeat the conclusion in every heading|Delete all material facts|Guarantee the desired remedy in the opening sentence|Neutral framing prevents the question from presupposing its answer.')
exam(23,'midterm','A draft treats an uncertain rule and an absent document as one research problem. What should its action plan distinguish?|Legal-source research from investigation of the missing fact|Only the memo font from its page size|A rule that both gaps automatically favour the client|An assumption that an absent document repeals the law|Different gaps require different evidence or authority work.')
exam(23,'midterm','During an interview the speaker changes a date after reviewing a receipt. What is the sound record?|Preserve the original account and correction with their sources|Silently erase the initial account|Treat the correction as automatic proof of fraud|Ignore the receipt to preserve a neat chronology|A transparent chronology records changes and the evidence explaining them.')
exam(23,'midterm','A case plan lists ten documents without explaining their relevance. What would improve it most?|Connect each requested record to an element or factual dispute|Request every available private record indiscriminately|Assume volume alone establishes proof|Replace documents with the interviewer conclusions|Targeted investigation connects information requests to the legal issues.')
exam(24,'midterm','An official acted within the right institution but allegedly denied a required hearing. Which analysis is still needed?|The procedural duty and consequence of the alleged denial|None because institutional identity proves legality|Only whether the outcome was popular|Whether a foreign rule automatically invalidates every decision|A correct decision-maker can still raise a distinct procedural issue.')
exam(24,'midterm','A requested order would substitute the learner’s preferred policy for a lawful discretionary choice. What must be established first?|A legal basis and defect supporting the court’s remedial intervention|The learner’s preference as sufficient review authority|A rule that all public discretion is unlawful|An assumption that disagreement creates damages|Judicial relief must rest on the governing powers and established legal defect.')
exam(24,'midterm','A proposed constitutional change has been discussed publicly but no formal adoption record is available. How should its status be described?|A proposal whose required legal stages must be verified|An effective amendment because discussion was extensive|A statute automatically overriding the Constitution|A judicial judgment without a court decision|Legal status depends on completion of the prescribed process.')
exam(24,'midterm','A civic complaint mixes assembly rights, candidate eligibility and vote counting. What makes the answer clearer?|Separate the rights and processes and source each applicable rule|Treat all three as one identical issue|Assume a candidate’s popularity resolves all questions|Apply one foreign electoral deadline to every stage|Distinct civic and electoral issues need distinct legal analysis.')
exam(25,'midterm','An interim application asks for ownership to be transferred before disputed title is determined. What should be scrutinised?|Whether the proposed protection prematurely grants final relief|Only whether the applicant used an urgent heading|A rule that interim proceedings always decide title|An assumption that temporary orders have unlimited scope|Protective relief must be distinguished from final adjudication.')
exam(25,'midterm','A proposed restraint cannot identify which equipment or act it covers. What is its practical and legal weakness?|Its scope is insufficiently defined for assessment and compliance|All restraints may lawfully remain vague|A broad request automatically covers every asset|A respondent’s uncertainty proves the merits|An operative order should state what it lawfully requires or prohibits.')
exam(25,'midterm','After judgment, part of a debt is paid and another order limits enforcement. What must the execution plan use?|The remaining obligation and effective orders together|The original amount with later records ignored|A rule that every payment vacates the entire judgment|The creditor’s preferred amount irrespective of orders|Execution must reflect the actual enforceable position.')
exam(25,'midterm','A creditor targets property held by someone not named as debtor. What must its analysis establish?|The lawful basis for reaching that property and relevant ownership|A universal power over all assets near the debtor|The creditor’s desire to recover quickly|A rule that any association establishes personal liability|Judgment execution must respect the relevant debtor and property rights.')
exam(26,'midterm','A later delivery note contradicts the signed contract and the buyer never accepted the new wording. What issue is primary?|Whether a valid variation or incorporated term changed the agreement|Whether every later document overrides all earlier terms|Whether delivery notes are always statutes|Whether the buyer’s silence conclusively proves every proposed term|The legal basis for changed obligations must be established.')
exam(26,'midterm','A clause limits responsibility for delay, while the claim concerns an inaccurate product description. What is required?|Interpret the clause’s actual scope against the particular claim|Assume any limitation defeats every claim|Treat descriptions as irrelevant once a clause exists|Ignore mandatory rules because wording is printed|A limitation’s effect depends on scope and the governing framework.')
exam(26,'midterm','A buyer alleges deception but signed after receiving the accurate technical record. What fact needs direct analysis?|What the buyer knew and relied upon when agreeing|Only whether the buyer later disliked the bargain|A rule that all sales include criminal deception|An assumption that any inaccurate statement makes a contract void|Knowledge and reliance can affect the formation-defect claim.')
exam(26,'midterm','A party seeks both unwinding and compensation without separating the legal bases. What improves the remedies discussion?|Analyse each remedy’s conditions, consequences and possible limits|Promise both automatically whenever a defect is alleged|Treat restoration and damages as the same calculation|Remove the underlying defect analysis|Distinct remedies require distinct legal and factual foundations.')
exam(27,'midterm','A business instructed an unsafe act and also disputes responsibility for its worker. What should be analysed?|Direct responsibility for instructions separately from vicarious liability|Only employment status as a universal answer|A rule that direct and vicarious theories cannot coexist|Only the worker’s preferred defendant|Different liability bases must be connected to their own elements.')
exam(27,'midterm','A premises claimant sues a registered owner although another person controlled the relevant hazard. What factual inquiry matters?|The allocation of control and applicable duties at the relevant time|A rule that ownership alone resolves every duty|Only the property’s market price|Whether the claimant prefers the owner|Premises responsibility depends on legally relevant roles and control.')
exam(27,'midterm','A post accurately quotes an allegation but presents it as a court finding. What should the publication analysis examine?|The actual communicated meaning and status of the claimed finding|Only whether quotation marks were used|A rule that attributing an allegation removes every risk|Whether all reported allegations are judgments|Context and represented factual status can affect meaning and legal analysis.')
exam(27,'midterm','A reputation claim includes lost customers but no record linking their departure to publication. What is missing?|Evidence supporting causation and the claimed recoverable loss|A more dramatic headline|An automatic foreign damages amount|A presumption that every business decline proves publication loss|A damages claim must connect its items to evidence and applicable rules.')
exam(28,'midterm','A proposed attempt analysis identifies intention but omits the statutory conduct threshold. What must be developed?|Whether the proved acts satisfy the governing requirement|A conclusion that intention proves every incomplete offence|A rule that no unsuccessful conduct can be criminal|The accused’s general reputation instead of acts|Attempt requires the applicable conduct and mental elements.')
exam(28,'midterm','An alleged conspiracy includes one person who learned of the plan only afterward. What is the key problem?|Proof of that person’s required agreement or participation cannot be assumed|Late knowledge automatically proves prior agreement|Every acquaintance shares the same mental state|An unsuccessful plan removes the need for individual evidence|Liability must be supported for each participant under the relevant offence.')
exam(28,'midterm','A cash custodian used funds for an authorised purchase that failed. Why investigate further before a theft conclusion?|Authority and mental elements may distinguish loss from criminal misuse|Any missing return proves theft automatically|Authorisation makes every later act immune from law|A business loss cannot raise any legal issue|The offence analysis needs more than the fact of financial loss.')
exam(28,'midterm','A property charge describes taking but not consent or the relevant entitlement. What should the elements chart add?|The legally required property interest, authority and mental questions|Only a list of the accused’s acquaintances|A rule that possession always proves ownership|A conclusion based solely on the complainant’s chosen label|The statutory offence controls which property and consent facts matter.')
exam(29,'midterm','The police account and formal charging instrument contain different dates. What is the sound procedural response?|Compare the actual requirements, records and legal effect of the discrepancy|Declare automatic guilt from either document|Privately edit the filed charge|Assume every discrepancy requires the same remedy|Charging issues must be evaluated under the applicable procedure.')
exam(29,'midterm','A disclosure request demands every record ever held by an investigator. What makes it more defensible?|Specify relevant categories and connect them to the case and governing duty|Add unrelated confidential records without explanation|Assume breadth alone proves entitlement|Replace lawful procedure with public pressure|A focused request identifies legal relevance and the applicable disclosure basis.')
exam(29,'midterm','An appeal ground names a possible error but no part of the record. What should be supplied?|A verifiable record reference and materiality analysis|A stronger assertion without evidence|A universal promise of release|A new accusation against all officials|Appellate reasoning must connect the asserted error to the actual decision and record.')
exam(29,'midterm','A new document is offered after conviction with an unknown author. What preliminary work matters?|Investigate authenticity, provenance and the authorised review route|Treat novelty as automatic reliability|Insert it secretly into the trial file|Assume every new document changes the burden of proof|New evidence must be assessed through lawful procedure and reliability safeguards.')
exam(30,'midterm','An expert’s conclusion depends on an assumed measurement never taken. What should examination address?|The assumption, method and effect on the opinion’s weight|Only the expert’s confidence|A rule that qualifications cure every missing measurement|The claimant’s preference for a technical answer|An opinion’s reliability depends on its factual and methodological basis.')
exam(30,'midterm','A factual witness is asked for a technical cause beyond their knowledge. What distinction matters?|Permitted factual testimony versus an expert opinion requiring its own basis|A rule that every eyewitness becomes an expert|The witness’s willingness to answer as sufficient expertise|An assumption that every inference is conclusive|The witness’s proper subject and admission conditions require attention.')
exam(30,'midterm','A confidential business email was not written for legal advice. What must be assessed separately?|Ethical handling duties and the conditions of any claimed legal privilege|A rule that every office email is privileged|A rule that confidentiality never creates any duty|The email’s font as its legal status|Confidentiality and privilege are distinct forms of protection.')
exam(30,'midterm','Counsel says evidence was unlawfully obtained but names no applicable consequence. What does the objection need?|The governing right or rule, relevant facts and requested ruling|A universal exclusion rule assumed for every country|A demand to decide the entire case by outrage|A private instruction to destroy the evidence|An objection must connect the alleged defect to its lawful procedural response.')
exam(31,'midterm','A tenant grants another business permanent rights over the landlord’s land. What must be checked?|The tenant’s actual interest and authority to grant that right|A rule that occupation alone gives full transfer powers|The sub-user’s willingness to pay as sufficient authority|The building’s condition as proof of title|A person can only grant rights within a lawful power or interest.')
exam(31,'midterm','Two co-owners disagree about a lease, and the instrument does not describe their authority. What is unresolved?|The governing powers and legally required consent for the transaction|A rule that the louder owner always decides|The assumption that shared property can never be used|A universal foreign co-ownership form|The recognised arrangement determines the participants’ powers.')
exam(31,'midterm','A survey matches a seller’s description but a competing title document appears. What is the prudent analysis?|Investigate both claims and the seller’s actual transferable interest|Assume matching boundaries prove exclusive title|Delete the competing record from the file|Use the surveyor’s signature as unlimited conveyance power|A precise description does not resolve competing legal rights.')
exam(31,'midterm','A community transaction record lists attendees but no decision or mandate. What must be verified?|The applicable participation, decision and representation requirements|Attendance as automatic consent to every term|A rule that an investor may appoint its own community representative|The proposed price alone as authority|A lawful community transaction needs the legally relevant process and authority.')

exam(22,'final','A public judgment is used for a different issue from the one necessary to its outcome. What must the final opinion clarify?|The limits of the holding and the status of the broader observation|That all printed text is equally controlling|That party submissions become statutes|That similarity of names determines precedent|Accurate precedent use requires context and decisional relevance.')
exam(22,'final','A mixed land-and-contract claim is sent to one forum without reviewing its powers. What is the missing institutional analysis?|Competence over each material component and their lawful relationship|An assumption that convenient location resolves every issue|A claim that all customary and judicial bodies are identical|A rule that a contract automatically removes all land questions|Mixed matters require a sourced forum analysis.')
exam(22,'final','A court guide copied from abroad gives a local magistrate a particular monetary limit. What should replace it?|Verified Liberian jurisdiction provisions applicable to the claim|A larger foreign limit chosen for convenience|The claim’s requested amount as automatic jurisdiction|A rule that all magistrates share one worldwide power|Local law determines subordinate-court competence.')
exam(23,'final','A draft opinion lists authorities but never links them to disputed facts. What is its central analytical deficiency?|The application and reasoned route to the conclusion are missing|Its bibliography contains too many primary sources|A reasoned opinion requires no counterargument|The facts should simply be removed|Legal reasoning must connect governing propositions to the material record.')
exam(23,'final','An interviewer writes “witness saw theft” after the speaker said a neighbour reported it. What correction is required?|Attribute the information to its actual source and knowledge status|Treat all repeated accounts as direct observation|Replace the statement with an invented admission|Assume a neat chronology makes source questions irrelevant|The file must distinguish firsthand knowledge from reported information.')
exam(23,'final','A memorandum omits an adverse rule found during research. What is the professional response?|Evaluate the adverse authority and explain its effect candidly|Suppress it because the memo supports a client|Replace it with an unverifiable quotation|Promise the reader that the preferred outcome is certain|Balanced predictive analysis requires accurate treatment of relevant adverse material.')
exam(24,'final','A regulator has a lawful objective but uses a power assigned to another institution. What issue should the challenge identify?|Legal competence for the particular act despite the objective|A rule that good intentions cure every power defect|Only whether the public likes the objective|An assumption that all regulation is unconstitutional|Purpose and lawful authority are distinct questions.')
exam(24,'final','A civic explainer calls a proposed amendment current law while formal stages remain incomplete. What needs correction?|The proposal’s legal status and the remaining prescribed process|The publication’s graphic colours only|A claim that discussion automatically repeals existing text|A rule that participation is never relevant|Current law and a proposal must not be conflated.')
exam(24,'final','A claimant requests constitutional compensation without proving harm or the remedial basis. What remains necessary?|The governing remedy conditions and supporting facts|A universal fixed award for every complaint|The claimant’s preference as a sufficient legal source|An assumption that review always means compensation|Relief must match the established violation and applicable powers.')
exam(25,'final','A protective application risks irreversible harm to a third party not considered in the draft. What should be added?|The applicable safeguards and a reasoned examination of that effect|A declaration that urgency removes all third-party interests|An instruction to conceal the risk|A request for every final remedy at once|Interim relief requires attention to scope and legally relevant competing interests.')
exam(25,'final','An appeal notice is mentioned in correspondence, but enforcement status is disputed. Which documents are decisive to investigate?|The actual filing, judgment and effective stay or subsequent orders|The creditor’s recollection alone|A foreign appeal leaflet as local proof|An assumption that any letter reverses judgment|The legal effect depends on the verified procedural record.')
exam(25,'final','An execution plan includes a debt already discharged in part. What should its calculation do?|Reconcile payments with the remaining enforceable obligation|Recover the original figure without adjustment|Treat every payment as unrelated to judgment|Seize unrelated assets to avoid reconciliation|Enforcement should reflect the obligation actually outstanding.')
exam(26,'final','A salesperson’s factual assurance and a written disclaimer appear in different formation stages. What must be analysed?|Their contractual or other legal status, chronology and applicable effect|A rule that every later printed disclaimer controls|A rule that oral statements always repeal legislation|Only which document has more pages|Formation and incorporation determine how the materials can affect the dispute.')
exam(26,'final','A rescission claim concerns property transferred to a third party. What issue deserves separate examination?|Any governing limit or protection affecting the proposed unwinding|A universal rule that third-party interests never matter|Automatic criminal guilt of the new holder|An assumption that damages and restoration are identical|The requested remedy must be assessed against relevant rights and conditions.')
exam(26,'final','A party alleges pressure because the other side negotiated firmly. What must the answer establish?|Conduct satisfying the actual legal test for the alleged consent defect|A rule that every firm negotiation is duress|Only that the bargain was later regretted|The speaker’s opinion as a complete legal test|Hard bargaining and legally improper pressure must be distinguished.')
exam(27,'final','A claimant combines premises injury and publication loss under one duty statement. What is the better structure?|Separate causes, elements, defendants and supported losses|Assume both claims have identical requirements|Treat every civil complaint as defamation|Use publication evidence as automatic proof of premises control|Distinct tort theories require their own factual and legal foundations.')
exam(27,'final','A company worker’s conduct occurred during a private departure from assigned activity. What should be researched?|The applicable connection test and the actual circumstances|A rule that employment proves liability for every act|A rule that any departure always defeats every claim|Only the claimant’s preferred defendant|The governing relationship and connection must be applied to the facts.')
exam(27,'final','A damages schedule uses estimated lost income without identifying its source. What revision is needed?|Explain the calculation, supporting records and legally relevant causal link|Increase the figure to make the claim serious|Copy an unrelated foreign award|Treat every estimate as a court finding|Recoverable loss needs a transparent evidential foundation.')
exam(28,'final','A person’s plan changed before any target offence was completed. What is the appropriate criminal method?|Apply the relevant incomplete-offence and withdrawal rules to the proved acts|Assume failed completion eliminates every offence|Assume discussion proves every possible charge|Assign group guilt without individual analysis|Incomplete offending requires its own statutory elements and individual evidence.')
exam(28,'final','A disputed payment was authorised, but investigators suspect a separate false representation. What must be separated?|Authority for payment from the elements of the alleged deception|A rule that authority cures every representation|A rule that any suspicion proves dishonesty|Civil loss from all questions of evidence|Distinct conduct and mental requirements should not be conflated.')
exam(28,'final','A prosecution summary states the offence label but omits its required mental element. What is incomplete?|The statutory elements and proof analysis|Only the document’s length|A rule that labels replace facts|An assumption that presence always proves intention|An offence must be established through the actual required conduct and mental state.')
exam(29,'final','A defence application requests relief unrelated to its stated charging defect. What should the drafter connect?|The governing defect, its legal effect and the authorised remedy|A demand for any outcome the accused prefers|A universal remedy copied from foreign procedure|The accusation’s seriousness as automatic relief|Procedural requests should match the rule and issue actually raised.')
exam(29,'final','A conviction challenge relies on a changed account without preserving the earlier statement. What should the review file do?|Record both accounts, their provenance and the proper route for assessing the change|Erase the earlier version permanently|Treat the new account as automatically conclusive|Insert the change into the original record secretly|Review requires a transparent account of evidence and procedural status.')
exam(29,'final','A proposed appeal asks the court to decide new facts without checking its powers. What is the necessary inquiry?|The authorised review scope, standard and record or new-evidence route|A rule that all appeals hear anything offered|Only whether the party prefers a fresh hearing|An assumption that every trial inconsistency mandates reversal|An appeal must fit the applicable procedural framework.')
exam(30,'final','A technical report uses a method outside the author’s demonstrated expertise. What should its analysis address?|Qualifications for that opinion, method and applicable admission rules|The author’s general confidence as a complete foundation|The report’s length as proof of expertise|A rule that all technical language is conclusive|The expertise must fit the particular opinion and governing requirements.')
exam(30,'final','A document contains public invoice details and a distinct legal-advice passage. What is the sound protection analysis?|Consider the components and their actual applicable protections separately|Treat every sentence as legally identical|Assume any invoice removes all privilege from a whole file|Use the folder’s label as the only legal test|Different content can raise different information and evidential protections.')
exam(30,'final','An objection names a legal rule but does not identify the offered item. What must be added?|The item and facts to which the rule is being applied|A demand to exclude the entire proceeding without analysis|A foreign judgment title instead of the relevant record|An assumption that the judge must guess the issue|A focused evidential ruling requires an identifiable item and legal basis.')
exam(31,'final','A deed, survey and community decision record concern slightly different land descriptions. What should a due-diligence memo do?|Reconcile the discrepancies and identify their effect on rights and authority|Select the neatest document and discard the others|Treat all descriptions as automatically equivalent|Assume a survey resolves every representation defect|Material inconsistencies must be investigated before a transaction conclusion.')
exam(31,'final','A seller offers rights beyond their verified interest in shared land. What is the legal question?|Whether the seller has authority to grant the particular proposed rights|Whether a buyer’s payment creates every missing power|Only whether the price is attractive|A rule that shared land always belongs to the first signer|Transfer authority must be tied to the actual legally recognised interest.')
exam(31,'final','A project has land permission but lacks a required operating authorisation. What should the final opinion distinguish?|Land rights from the independent regulatory requirements|A rule that permission to occupy licenses all activities|A rule that operating approval automatically proves ownership|The assumption that all approvals have identical purposes|Different authorisations serve different legal functions.')
exam(32,'final','A beneficiary demands immediate distribution before estate debts and authority are examined. What should the adviser explain?|Administration must establish assets, obligations and lawful representation first|Family preference automatically discharges every creditor|Every relative can distribute disputed property|A foreign inheritance video fixes all local shares|Distribution depends on the lawful administration framework and verified estate position.')
exam(32,'final','A manager holds funds for beneficiaries but uses them for an undisclosed personal investment. What needs analysis?|The governing powers, fiduciary conflict and account of the transaction|Only whether eventual profit is possible|A rule that legal administration equals personal ownership|An assumption that beneficiaries can never seek an account|The purpose and duties of administration limit personal use.')
exam(32,'final','A succession opinion relies on an unsigned document without examining execution. What is its unresolved foundation?|Whether the testamentary instrument satisfies the applicable validity requirements|A rule that its heading alone proves validity|An automatic assumption of equal intestate shares|The author’s family position as conclusive law|A claimed will’s validity must be established before its effect is applied.')
exam(33,'final','A pay claim includes contract wages, deducted amounts and leave issues in one figure. What is needed?|Separate legal bases and a reconciliation of each component|An assumption that every absence has identical legal treatment|A foreign minimum rate used without local verification|A claim that deductions never need explanation|Employment entitlements must be analysed by their actual rules and records.')
exam(33,'final','A workplace agreement is said to bind all workers, but representation and approval are unclear. What must be verified?|The mandate and applicable requirements giving the instrument legal effect|Only how many pages it contains|A rule that any discussion binds every worker|A rule that collective terms automatically repeal statutes|Collective effect requires legally sufficient representation and process.')
exam(33,'final','A safety plan supplies gloves but ignores a documented unguarded machine. What should the analysis add?|Controls addressing the actual hazard and residual risk under the governing duties|A rule that equipment alone removes every safety obligation|A waiver treated as permission for any risk|A demand to wait for a completed injury before considering prevention|Effective protection examines the source of the hazard, not equipment alone.')
exam(34,'final','An incorporated enterprise lacks authority records for a related-party transaction. What is the remaining corporate inquiry?|Competent approval, conflict duties and transaction authority|A rule that incorporation validates every later act|A rule that founder status creates unlimited power|Only whether the transaction looks profitable|Entity existence and the legality of a particular decision are separate matters.')
exam(34,'final','A partner’s departure leaves customer contracts unfinished. What should a winding-up plan address?|Remaining obligations, assets, authority and lawful completion or resolution|Only removing the company sign|A rule that closure cancels all outsider rights|An assumption that every participant has identical powers|Ending a relationship does not settle its outstanding affairs automatically.')
exam(34,'final','A company registers its name and claims professional authorisation to practise law. What is missing?|The separate professional qualifications and lawful authority required|Only a more elaborate logo|A rule that business registration grants every professional licence|A claim that a TIH completion certificate is a practising certificate|Entity registration does not authorise reserved professional activity.')
exam(35,'final','A goods contract identifies ownership transfer but is silent on transit damage. What still requires analysis?|Risk allocation under the applicable rules and agreement|An assumption that ownership and every risk are identical|A rule that possession eliminates all obligations|A foreign slogan as conclusive local law|Title and risk address distinct legal questions.')
exam(35,'final','Creditors disagree over equipment allegedly subject to security. What should the ranking analysis establish?|The valid rights, governing process and applicable priority conditions|A rule that whoever complains first wins|A rule that all registered entries cure every defect|The debtor’s preferred order as sufficient authority|Priority must rest on legally effective rights and the relevant framework.')
exam(35,'final','An insolvent company’s owner pays a related person while other claims remain. What is the proper first legal assessment?|Investigate the transaction and any applicable review or distribution rules|Declare guilt solely from the relationship|Assume ownership makes every payment immune|Ignore the transaction because the recipient is familiar|The effect depends on authority, timing, rights and governing conditions.')
exam(36,'final','An evaluation changes the stated criteria after bids arrive. What issue should the accountability review examine?|Consistency with the governing procurement duties and decision record|Only whether the winner’s price is convenient|A rule that evaluators may always invent later criteria|An assumption that cheaper bids justify every process defect|Lawful evaluation must be supported by the applicable rules and transparent record.')
exam(36,'final','A tax objection presents cancelled invoices but never cites their governing treatment. What is incomplete?|The connection between documentary facts and the applicable tax rule|Only the number of attachments|A rule that cancellation always means exemption|The taxpayer’s desire for a lower amount as a complete ground|Evidence needs a relevant legal basis for the proposed adjustment.')
exam(36,'final','A current procurement question uses an older threshold without checking the 2026 instruments. What is the main research risk?|The rule applied may be outdated or inapplicable to the transaction|Older text is always meaningless in full|A comparative video supplies the correct local amount|Every public contract uses one worldwide threshold|Status, commencement and applicability must be verified.')
exam(37,'final','A regional complaint is procedurally eligible but disputed on the underlying facts. What must the writer keep distinct?|Admissibility and the merits of the alleged violation|A rule that eligibility proves the violation|A rule that a complaint form is a domestic judgment|An assumption that all institutions have identical remedies|Acceptance for consideration does not establish the substantive claim.')
exam(37,'final','A cross-border agreement names the law but leaves the court and enforcement route open. What must the memo separate?|Governing law, jurisdiction and recognition or execution|A rule that naming law decides every forum question|An assumption that any foreign decision is immediately executable|A rule that contracts eliminate court competence|Different cross-border questions require their own legal source and analysis.')
exam(37,'final','A foreign judgment is presented without proof of its authentic terms or notice record. What should be requested?|The judgment and relevant procedural records for the local recognition analysis|A private seizure instruction|A foreign news report as equivalent proof|An assumption that the creditor’s summary decides every condition|Local effect must be tested using the actual decision and required supporting record.')
exam(38,'final','A cargo claimant sues a vessel owner solely because the vessel is Liberian-flagged. What is the missing responsibility analysis?|The contractual and regulatory roles relevant to the alleged loss|A rule that the flag identifies every carriage promise|A rule that owners, carriers and charterers are always interchangeable|The port photograph as proof of contractual liability|Maritime claims need the actual obligation and legally relevant party connection.')
exam(38,'final','An insurer has paid part of a covered loss and another party may be responsible. What must the recovery analysis reconcile?|Compensated loss, remaining loss and applicable recovery rights|An unrestricted right to collect the same full loss repeatedly|Only which payer is wealthier|A rule that premium payment transfers every claim automatically|Indemnity and subsequent recovery must avoid unsupported double counting.')
exam(38,'final','A coverage opinion uses only a policy advertisement rather than its complete wording. What is required?|The actual insuring terms, conditions, exclusions and facts of the event|A promise that marketing language settles every limit|A universal rule that all policies cover all losses|Only the premium receipt as proof of every condition|Coverage depends on the governing policy and legal framework.')
exam(39,'final','A project’s actual operations exceed the activity described in its assessment. What must be checked?|The approval’s scope, conditions and applicable requirements for the change|A rule that one report permits any later operation|A rule that incorporation replaces environmental approval|Only the project’s economic benefit|Assessment and authorisation must be matched to the activity actually undertaken.')
exam(39,'final','A startup owns a device but cannot identify the creator or rights agreement. What must its IP audit distinguish?|Possession of the object from ownership and permission relating to IP rights|A rule that all physical ownership creates patents|An assumption that payment transfers every possible right|A rule that every idea is a registered trademark|Physical assets, legal rights and licences require separate analysis.')
exam(39,'final','A website credits a photographer but lacks permission for commercial modification. What remains unresolved?|Whether the applicable rights and licence authorise the intended use|A rule that credit always permits modification|A rule that downloading makes the image public domain|A company name registration as an image licence|Attribution and permission serve different legal functions.')
exam(40,'final','An advocate learns adverse authority is directly relevant to the submitted position. What is the proper course?|Address it accurately and develop any supported distinction|Invent a quotation favouring the client|Hide its relevance from the court|Assume fees justify any omission|Professional candour requires accurate engagement with material authority.')
exam(40,'final','An appellate argument asks for relief beyond the reviewing court’s established powers. What should be revised?|The requested order to fit the supported issue and lawful remedial scope|Only the speech’s emotional emphasis|A rule that any error authorises any order|A claim that oral confidence creates jurisdiction|Relief must be connected to the court’s actual powers and established error.')
exam(40,'final','A professional proposes using another person’s entrusted money without authority. What is the key duty issue?|Lawful control, permitted use and accountability for the funds|Only whether the loan is intended to be short|A rule that future repayment guarantees permission|An assumption that trust makes records unnecessary|Funds held for others remain subject to their governing authority and duties.')
exam(41,'final','A jurisprudence essay says legal validity automatically proves moral justice. What must be separated?|Recognition within the legal system from moral evaluation|Only legal vocabulary from spelling|A rule that all theories are statutes|An assumption that moral opinion immediately repeals law|Validity and justification are different analytical questions.')
exam(41,'final','A losing arbitration party requests a full rehearing without identifying an authorised ground. What must its application establish?|The applicable challenge ground and proper process|A universal right to retry every award on the merits|A rule that no court may ever examine an award|Only the party’s dissatisfaction|Court intervention depends on the governing arbitral and procedural framework.')
exam(41,'final','A learner completes the full TIH programme and its final examination. What does that establish?|Completion of this independent TIH educational programme|Automatic admission to the Liberian Bar|A university law degree issued by TIH|Authority to provide reserved legal services without further qualification|The programme’s completion credential does not replace academic or professional authorisation.')
